# Entry Main. A named actual whose name is no input of the real parent of the selected record admits no form: the
# record is refused before its right-hand side is read.
# Step 21.7 K2, S3: `p` selects Model (the reference place p of D holds Model), and the data is the real parent of the
# selected record. The named actual `v := data\other` names v: v lies inside Model, and the real parent of Model has
# no input v. The binder refuses the form: 5, before the value of the actual is read -- the missing selector
# `data\other` is never reached. The reference p is read by an explicit write before the launch (prepared_p 1); Model
# is not changed (v 1). The reached missing selector of a form that is admitted is checked by
# place_missing_selector_reached.
# Norm: the book #declaration-selection (the inputs are described by the data parent(C); a name without an input is no
# form), #structural-call.
Model:
    int: v 1
end: Model
D:
    @: p Model
    Attempt:
        p(v := data\other)
    end: Attempt
end: D
Observed:
    int: before 0
    int: prepared_p 0
end: Observed
Main:
    Observed\before := 1
    Observed\prepared_p := D\p\v
    D\Attempt()
